And then people start painting on top of it.

“Turn an equation into a scene” begins as a doorway to Math to Myth. Then one person writes a comedy sketch, another uses the method to teach algebra, and a third contributes an equation that breaks the method. Now the Pantheon has a workshop where it used to have a link. The doorway helped bring the workshop into being.

That’s the deeper connection between semantic surface area and platforming. A phrase makes a possibility visible. An example makes it repeatable. When people build on each other’s examples, the possibility becomes a place where work happens.

It also means naming something in the repo is a design decision. Put “Turn an equation into a scene” in the index and you invite one kind of contribution. Put “Find a mathematical relationship that makes a better plot” beside it and you invite another. The same artifact can grow two different neighborhoods, depending on what people are invited to do there.